Z||000001||Kasdan||09-07-2001||06:01 PM||||My guess is a thrown rod...maybe a pushrod, maybe a piston rod.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-08-2001||10:11 AM||||Do you have any idea what oil the seller put in it?  Chances are he/she was trying to quiet the knock with heavier grade oil so the oil pressure is okay.  If it is the typical 'rod knock', it will be a rod bearing.  Be careful driving an engine with a knock as it may be salvageable now but may not be if you continue to run it.  GL||||reg||1
